              <p class="kicker">Overview</p>
              <h2>An overview of <em>where you're going</em>.</h2>
              <p class="lead dropcap">Ladakh sits where the Himalayas meet the Karakoram, a high-altitude cold desert that for centuries has held one of the most contemplative cultures on earth. Buddhist monasteries cling to cliffs above villages whose names sound like prayers. The light here is famously sharp, the silences famously long.</p>
              <p>From Leh, the regional capital, you can reach the moonscapes of Nubra, the lunar lakes of Pangong and Tso Moriri, the high passes of Khardung La, and a string of monasteries — Thiksey, Hemis, Diskit — that anchor any first-time itinerary.</p>
            </div>

